This is a small reusable library, not a full application. So we are keeping the public API in one root package and creating only one private writer folder for implementation details.

Current structure:

iva-session-storage/
  types.go              Public types
  writer.go             Public write/save workflow
  errors.go             Shared public errors
  writer_test.go        Writer behavior tests
  README.md
  go.mod
  go.sum

  internal/
    writer/
      validation.go     Private writer input validation
      dynamodb.go       Private DynamoDB UpdateItem request helpers

The root package is what other applications import:

  import sessionstorage "iva-session-storage"

The internal/writer folder is private implementation code. Callers should not import it directly.

We are avoiding application-style folders like service/, repository/, models/, and handlers/ because those are more suitable for full applications. This module is a small shared library.
